    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f0169f77_7b215ff1",
        "filename": "ansible/roles/prep-kubespray/files/multus_network/patches/network_plugin/main.yml.patch",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 10,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000416
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-03-05T10:28:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Multus can provide multiple CNI for kubernetes. After discussion with gopi, we will use the calico-CNI as the default network and add the ovs-CNI as a additional network.\nSo, We should also install the calico components into the kubernetes,  there\u0027re two way that we can do it.\n1. We write a new ansible files to install all calico components by ourself and put those files under the multus directory.\n2. Use the existing calico script to help us install the calico.\n\nIn order to decrease the complexity of the script, I choose use solution (2) to handle this, so we should run the calico scripts if we choose the multus network.",
      "parentUuid": "69a94c77_ed1c7541",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 6,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 10,
        "endChar": 15
      },
